  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(F=\\dfrac{6x^2+16x+3m}{6}\\) be the square of an expression which is linear in \\(x.\\) Then \\(m\\) has a particular value between:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3\\) and \\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4\\) and \\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(5\\) and \\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-4\\) and \\(-3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(-6\\) and \\(-5\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\[ F=x^2+\\frac83x+\\frac m2. \\] For this to be a square, it must equal \\((x+\\frac{4}{3})^2,\\) whose constant term is \\(\\frac{16}{9}.\\) Hence \\(\\frac{m}{2}=\\frac{16}{9},\\) so \\(m=\\frac{32}{9},\\) which lies between \\(3\\) and \\(4.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(F=x^2+\\frac83x+\\frac m2\\)",
        "Match the constant term to the square of half the linear coefficient"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
